"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Can computed capsid–receptor binding calls for ALPL, AAVR and LRP6 reproduce published bind/no-bind readouts with interfaces at the threefold axis?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Pairs that bind in plate- and bead-based assays share threefold-axis or insert-loop engagement geometry, so pose enumeration recovers published bind/no-bind labels [s_aavr_struct].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_aavr_struct\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41564-018-0356-7\",\"quote\":\"This structure reveals that of the five Ig-like polycystic kidney disease (PKD) domains in AAVR, PKD2 binds directly to the spike region of the AAV2 capsid adjacent to the icosahedral three-fold axis.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Balanced accuracy 0.80 at 432 runs versus 0.55 at 54, with five of six known binders within 5 Å of published sites.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Accuracy moves under 0.05 between 54 and 432 runs and at most three of six binders reach published sites; extra runs resample the wrong basin.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Thirty-six capsid–receptor pairs run docking, three AlphaFold-Multimer seeds, two 5-ns MD relaxations; calls and threefold-site geometry scored on published labels; parallel wall-clock versus serial one-GPU and independent-copy baselines.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Shay and colleagues in 2024 ran five AlphaFold-Multimer models per peptide and used cryo-ET to map where LRP6 and IL3 bind engineered capsids, with SPR binding labels [s_shay_af].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_shay_af\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-024-52149-0/figures/4\",\"quote\":\"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\"}],\"value\":10}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Whether hundreds of pose and seed runs improve bind/no-bind agreement with threefold-axis geometry across a full capsid-by-receptor grid remains untested [s_shay_af].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_shay_af\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-024-52149-0/figures/4\",\"quote\":\"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Redocking AAVR-PKD2 onto AAV2 must place it beside the threefold spike matching PDB 6IHB contacts; serial and parallel pilots must match calls.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_aavr_struct\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41564-018-0356-7\",\"quote\":\"This structure reveals that of the five Ig-like polycystic kidney disease (PKD) domains in AAVR, PKD2 binds directly to the spike region of the AAV2 capsid adjacent to the icosahedral three-fold axis.\"}],\"value\":\"PKD2 bound to the AAV2 spike region adjacent to the icosahedral three-fold axis (PDB 6IHB)\"}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Binding-call agreement and interface geometry only; no transcytosis or affinity. Public labels cover 13 of 36 pairs; NR001–NR005 and Starfish assays are proprietary.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_aavr_struct\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41564-018-0356-7\",\"quote\":\"This structure reveals that of the five Ig-like polycystic kidney disease (PKD) domains in AAVR, PKD2 binds directly to the spike region of the AAV2 capsid adjacent to the icosahedral three-fold axis.\",\"supports\":\"Anchor geometry: AAVR-PKD2 engagement at the AAV2 threefold-adjacent spike, structure PDB 6IHB.\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_shay_af\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-024-52149-0/figures/4\",\"quote\":\"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\",\"supports\":\"Closest prior compute quantity (AlphaFold model count and recycle depth) and the E1E2-versus-E3E4 domain check used as an anchor.\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:af2_h_per_run\",\"name\":\"Wall-clock hours for one AlphaFold-Multimer run on one A100\",\"value\":0.5,\"unit\":\"GPU_h_per_run\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"Prediction time for a structure of N residues is roughly (N/30)*(N/30) seconds for an Nvidia A40 GPU.\",\"page_setting\":\"ColabFold single-structure prediction on one Nvidia A40\",\"differs_in\":[\"monomer timing formula, not a 750–1000-residue hetero-multimer with 5 models and up to 20 recycles\",\"Lambda A100 SXM 40 GB instead of an A40\"],\"url\":\"https://www.rbvi.ucsf.edu/chimerax/data/wynton-colabfold-feb2024/colabfold_wynton.html\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:md_ns_per_day_a100\",\"name\":\"GROMACS throughput on one A100\",\"value\":129,\"unit\":\"ns_per_day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"a protein in explicit water (170,320 atoms) ... | A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2 |\",\"page_setting\":\"GROMACS 2024.1 benchmark system 4 (170,320-atom protein in explicit water) on one A100, reported in ns/day\",\"differs_in\":[\"our system is a docked capsid–receptor complex in explicit solvent, roughly 120k–180k atoms\",\"Lambda A100 SXM 40 GB\"],\"url\":\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\"}

